      "summary": "Estimated increase of $546,761 general fund in FY2027, rising sharply to $14M general fund in FY2028 and over $38M by FY2031. The dramatic growth is driven almost entirely by Medicaid (DMAS): the $15.00/hr wage in FY2028 exceeds the current Medicaid attendant care rate of $13.88/hr, requiring the state to raise wages for approximately 80,000 home care workers whose pay is set by Medicaid reimbursement rates. FY2027 costs are modest because the $13.75/hr rate stays below the current $13.88/hr Medicaid rate, so no Medicaid adjustment is needed that year. In short, the cost is not a direct government payroll expense — it is the state's share of higher Medicaid reimbursements paid to home care providers.",
